  story:[ "<b>Fine sugar coats the wreckage like pale snow.</b> Bent duct panels point outward, and a motor cabinet bears one concentrated arc mark.", "Sweeper Ruiz, The Electrician, and The Clerk know the deposits, airflow, electrical equipment, and decisions behind the mill's last production run.", "Investigators are being pulled toward <b>Sabotage or a bomb</b> or <b>A freak spark — bad luck</b>. Both can be stated without opening a single cleaning log.", "Demolition begins in eight days. Once the upper galleries come down, the depth and spread of the deposits will be impossible to reconstruct." ],
  endings:{ overclaimWhat:"attack", dismissalWhat:"freak",
    win:{ expertTitle:"The Secondary Explosion Explained", expert:["You identify <b>Corwin Ash — plant owner</b>, <b>The Owner's Plant Office</b>, and <b>Cut housekeeping & ventilation, with dust left to accumulate</b>. Not sabotage or a bomb. Not a freak spark — bad luck. Deposit depth, stopped extraction, ignition evidence, and outward blast paths explain the mill sequence.","Your finding distinguishes the initiating spark from the much larger fuel inventory lifted from floors, beams, and ducts."], soundTitle:"A Combustible Finding", sound:["You connect <b>Corwin Ash — plant owner</b>, <b>The Owner's Plant Office</b>, and <b>Cut housekeeping & ventilation, with dust left to accumulate</b>. The dust mechanism is sound, although venting and secondary propagation receive limited detail.","The mill commission accepts the result because physical deposits, airflow records, and staffing decisions corroborate each other."], namedTitle:"The Dust Hazard Named", named:["You choose <b>Corwin Ash — plant owner</b>, <b>The Owner's Plant Office</b>, and <b>Cut housekeeping & ventilation, with dust left to accumulate</b>, but outline rather than demonstrate the floor-to-floor propagation.","The accusation remains correct; rebuilding standards still need measured explosibility and hidden-surface inventories."] },
    overclaim:{ title:"Bomb Language Replaces Combustion", body:["You select <b>Sabotage or a bomb</b>, yet the blast pattern and accumulated powder require no planted explosive to explain the pressure damage.","The bomb claim makes <b>Cut housekeeping & ventilation, with dust left to accumulate</b> sound less credible even though neglected fuel and ventilation are documented throughout the mill."] },
    dismissal:{ title:"The Spark Excuses the Fuel", body:["You accept <b>A freak spark — bad luck</b>, treating ignition as random while ignoring the preventable dust cloud waiting for any competent source.","That conclusion restores production without the cleaning, extraction, isolation, and grounding needed to stop recurrence."] },
    wrongNames:{ title:"Combustion Correct, Management Trail Wrong", body:["You establish <b>Cut housekeeping & ventilation, with dust left to accumulate</b> but attach the decisive choice or location incorrectly. The housekeeping authority leads to"] } },
